  "question": {
    "text": "For a particle in uniform circular motion, the acceleration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> at any point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> on the circular path of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is (when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> is measured from the positive <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> is uniform speed):"
  },
